--- MESSAGE ---
Option becomes Presence on the loader path: one conversion at the host boundary, then fold

DefinitionPath.source and TypeLoader's readDefinition, loadFromResource and tryLoad declare
`draco.drake.Presence(T)` in place of the host's Option. Each converts once, where the host produced the
optional value, through the declared symbol `presence`, which the Scala target renders as a match into
Present or Absent typed by the declared result; past the boundary the definition chains with `fold`,
never a host combinator. Dictionary.get keeps Option because it overrides the host's Map.get. The first
host head to take a target-neutral form; ActorRef, Consumer, LazyList and the Java lists follow, each
surfaced first.

